I recently compiled nethack on my Sparc 1+ running SunOS 4.1.1.  I had not
had any problems, but I noticed that it was not always finding the compress
program.  So I went into config.h and changed "COMPRESS=/usr/local/compress"
to "COMPRESS=/usr/ucb/compress".  It seemed the reasonable thing to do.
Everything seems to work fine, except files of the form "alock.n" are now
created, which have two obvious effects.  One, they keep other players from
entering level "n" when the lockfile belonging to me exists.  Two, they
cause me to die of "a trickery" when I remove them and then try to return
to a previous level.  I have grepped the word lock on the source and include
files, and the following files seem applicable: unixconf.h, do.c, end.c,
getline.c, unixmain.c and unixunix.c.  Unfortunately, I have finals this
week and don't have time to slog throught the source and find out what, if
anything is wrong.

Questions are: 1) Is the generation of these files normal, and why did I not
	notice it before? and 2) If it is not normal, how do I get rid of it?

Thanks in advance as I need the stress reduction right now and I am also
having a competition with some other people for the high score, so we all
need to be able to play, simultaneously if necessary.  The lock files are
removed if I die or quit, but not if I save or am still playing.
